WEBVTT

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:51.510
Mesopotamia...

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.320
Greek for "between the rivers."

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:58.760
Being here, I feel like I can see that the Great Flood of Noah really occurred.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:02.220
This was also a setting in the Old Testament after all, wasn't it?

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:07.060
In the end, perhaps you could call our workplace a Tower of Babel.

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:11.600
We're defying God and trying to grasp eternal life.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:16.980
It just came into sight. That's it there.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:23.520
Heaven's Gate...

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:28.590
A concentration of the wisdom of humankind, born in the cradle of civilization.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:42.230
It was there that you met the originals of all of us then?

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.800
That's right.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:57.150
Dispatched to Heaven's Gate,

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:00.520
...I was involved in research on the Gilgamesh experimental subjects,

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:05.230
...in order to seek out the secrets of eternal life from the genetic material of the gods.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.800
You were the ones working with me there.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:19.010
We were all young, but very brilliant scientists.

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:26.650
We were a very good team, helping one another not only on research and experiments,

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:29.380
...but also in our everyday lives as a whole.

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:35.360
The Heaven's Gate research was steadily producing results in every branch of science.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.230
Until that being was born inside Delphys, that is.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:42.700
You mean Tear?

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:47.500
Cases where experiments had formed matter or antimatter...

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.130
...had also been reported before that time.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:55.740
But a life form... that was a first.

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:02.490
Presently, it became clear that its light was contaminating everything in Heaven's Gate.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:13.630
The one who had been insisting all along that the Delphys research held dangers was Dr. Terumichi Madoka.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:18.670
The validity of the paper he had written was acknowledged,

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:23.300
...and the decision was made to destroy all the experimental subjects and close Heaven's Gate.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:30.110
It was a few days later that an emergency call echoed through Heaven's Gate.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:35.350
Dr. Madoka was the one who intruded into the main plant.

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:41.060
Ultimately, Delphys generated a tremendous explosion that encompassed the whole of Heaven's Gate.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:42.750
That was XX.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:46.360
Why would Dr. Madoka do such a thing?

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:47.790
I don't know.

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:51.900
It was some years later that I awoke from a dark sleep.

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:56.400
The world had been transformed, the sky veiled by a mirror.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:02.880
When was it that you married the Count of Werdenberg?

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:08.510
Shortly before XX. He was also a Heaven's Gate scientist.

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:17.190
My husband also died in XX, and I inherited a large fortune.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:25.500
I vowed I would use it to investigate the truth about the incident,

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:27.770
...to gain some closure for the years I had lost,

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:35.300
...since I was the only one who was involved in that great catastrophe and survived.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:39.080
It was some time afterwards that rumors began to circulate...

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:44.080
...about children bearing the paranormal powers called Dynamis.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:48.790
They came to be called Orga Superior.

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:58.800
I already know that we were born from the cloned embryos from Orga which were contaminated by Tear.

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:02.240
And how we were born, as well.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:04.840
I see.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:09.480
Why did you search us out?

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:12.410
Why didn't you just leave us alone?

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:17.580
Because I believed it was my mission to do so.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:21.290
When I found all of you,

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:25.960
...it was just as though I had been able to reunite with my own children.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:28.290
I felt a tremor in my heart.

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:54.220
I've never been able to forget the day I first met you either.

00:06:56.590 --> 00:06:59.260
I could hardly believe someone so beautiful existed.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.730
Fu was saying the same sort of thing,

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:06.870
...since she'd been through even worse than I had.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:13.070
She said when she saw you for the first time, it was just like she was dreaming.

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:26.780
Then Toru came, and all of us ended up living together in this hotel.

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:31.890
That's right, because we're a family.

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:37.230
I thought so too, until recently.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:45.570
This may be the last time I ever have a meal with you.

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:48.740
Why?

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:52.680
Because you're still concealing something.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:59.280
I'm not concealing anything.

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:04.530
I wonder about that.

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:08.760
It was foolish, wasn't it?

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:15.600
Thinking I might even be able to die for your sake...

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:56.580
They asked you too, didn't they?

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:01.890
Even if I went home now, I'd only be a burden on my mother.

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:04.150
I see.

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.870
<i>Hey, shall I take a picture for you?</i>

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:26.510
What's the matter? A cute girl like you, standing all alone?

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:30.240
It's because I don't like crowds very much.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:33.080
You're like me then.

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:36.490
You're a very brilliant student, aren't you?

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:40.390
The older men say you're a genius.

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:43.160
A genius, huh?

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:45.700
Do I look it?

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:46.660
Nope.

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:49.030
Well, what do I look like?

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:51.470
You look like you fool around a lot.

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:53.900
I'm flattered you'd say that.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:03.250
You look prettiest when you smile.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:20.420
That's the person who discovered Delphys.

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:23.890
He's Heaven's Gate's greatest genius.

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:29.100
But ever since the report he submitted was suppressed by the executive board,

00:10:29.510 --> 00:10:33.070
...he just plays the piano every day like that without participating in any project.

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:38.040
But that report rejects very the meaning of this place's existence, doesn't it?

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:41.980
I'd say its being suppressed was a foregone conclusion.

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:46.720
Hay fever in the middle of the desert?

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:49.360
I'm just gonna wash my face.

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:00.030
Hey, he's here, he's here!

00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:03.300
Dr. Madoka, hurry up!

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:04.900
Over here!

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:08.510
Sorry I'm late.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:11.640
Everyone, look this way, please!

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:15.090
You look prettiest when you smile.

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:18.120
All right, here we go!

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:20.720
'Scuse me.

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:24.890
Proton decay?

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:30.790
Its rate has been sped up by our interfering with Delphys.

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:34.330
If we continue as we are,

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:37.160
...it could even lead to the destruction of the Earth,

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:40.440
...because all matter will begin to decay.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:43.610
This is Delphys we're talking about.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:48.010
Before things come to that, it may set some kind of trap for us.

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:51.020
"Some kind..." What kind?

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:52.890
That's not clear even to me.

00:11:53.390 --> 00:11:58.200
This has already moved into the field of religion, more than what you'd call science.

00:11:58.460 --> 00:12:02.160
It's because Delphys is also linked to human hearts.

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:14.780
Are you wondering whose child it is?

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:15.910
No...

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:22.520
It's nobody's. It's my own clone, using the embryo from Orga.

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:30.690
It's sad when, in the end, the only one you can trust is yourself.

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:36.770
You'll end up like me too, if you keep being so passionate about someone who has a wife and child.

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:37.730
Well, I'm off.

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:41.500
I'll let you know when she's born.

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:05.130
She's my daughter.

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:16.540
This is my wife. My colleague, Kageyama.

00:13:18.510 --> 00:13:21.210
Oh, you remember, I told you before.

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:23.210
When I was a student...

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:28.880
Oh! The middle-school girl who told Terumichi he looked like he fooled around a lot!

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:31.250
He does, doesn't he?

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.560
Terumichi here doesn't look like a scientist or anything, huh?

00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:37.950
It's not just me who thinks so after all.

00:13:38.530 --> 00:13:39.720
Hey!

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:16.390
Kagami?

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:17.960
Yes...

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:19.570
Are you drunk?

00:14:19.570 --> 00:14:23.440
A bit. Congratulations on your engagement.

00:14:24.310 --> 00:14:25.640
Thanks.

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:30.410
At this place, he's a mere researcher, but originally he's nobility.

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:33.010
I hear when he goes back to his homeland, he's a count.

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:36.620
That makes you a countess as well.

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:38.590
Leave off with that.

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:41.850
For some reason, being here puts me at ease.

00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:44.190
I wonder if that's because it's connected to Delphys?

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:49.230
You're aware that a new life form has been discovered in the main plant,

00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:51.290
...I take it?

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:53.160
You mean Tear, right?

00:14:54.610 --> 00:14:58.060
I just hope it's not a trap Delphys has laid for us.

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:05.580
Tear... that name was aptly given.

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:12.880
A conclusion has been reached about the pending concern.

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:16.120
I will now present it to you.

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:20.820
All Heaven's Gate projects will be discontinued.

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:28.030
Delphys will be totally sealed off, all experimental subjects destroyed,

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:31.040
...and this facility closed down within the year.

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:37.710
Then you're saying what was written in Dr. Madoka's report was all correct?

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:41.150
We feel justified in concluding so.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:01.090
I thought I'd play this for Delphys.

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:04.940
If it's to be the last, it should be this piece.

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:16.210
It all turned out as you said... everything.

00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:19.950
This is where Gilgamesh's tomb was.

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:26.630
I think that stood as a symbol for all of this.

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:50.950
There's a problem in the underground facility!

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:56.080
The main plant?

00:16:56.490 --> 00:17:00.900
It's the remaining test subjects! Lot number T-e-Ar.

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:02.270
Tear!

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:03.670
That's preposterous!

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:05.440
It couldn't be terrorism, could it?

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:09.900
We've got an ID on the intruder. It's Dr. Terumichi Madoka.

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:12.140
Can we communicate directly with him?

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:15.670
Dr. Madoka! Turn back immediately! This is dangerous!

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:18.210
Do you know what you're doing?

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:20.650
He'll reach Delphys shortly!

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:23.440
This will be a disaster!

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:25.760
Stop him at all costs!

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:27.660
He's going through the physical lockdowns one after another!

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:30.850
Twenty more seconds to Delphys!

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:36.060
Dr. Madoka...

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:46.410
So this is the end...

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:00.550
So you have awakened.

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:12.170
My lady, you have remained asleep for a number of years, hovering on the line between life and death, after Twin X.

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:15.140
Twin... X?

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:22.670
That is how everyone refers to that great explosion at Heaven's Gate and the chaos that followed it, my lady.

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:27.420
I am steward to the House of Werdenberg, my lady.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:33.420
His Lordship too, went the way of all flesh in XX, and you, his wife,

00:18:33.620 --> 00:18:36.750
...are first in the line of succession to this House.

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:45.800
Now, why don't we have you begin by telling us about Dr. Madoka?

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:49.810
One would have to call him a genius.

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:52.610
I have great respect for him as a scientist.

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:57.110
We have received testimony that you and he had a relationship as lovers.

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:59.750
Who was it?! Who said such a thing?!

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:01.690
I am not at liberty to answer that.

00:19:01.690 --> 00:19:05.880
To say we were lovers is an insult to his wife, is it not?!

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:10.020
That wife of his continues to flee from this council's subpoena.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:14.400
She is now apparently living in horrible circumstances, with her young child in tow.

00:19:14.700 --> 00:19:19.830
From the looks of things though, she doesn't have any ideological background conducive to involvement in terrorism.

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:21.170
Terrorism?

00:19:21.170 --> 00:19:27.540
After XX, Terumichi Madoka took the name "Enkidu," and has claimed responsibility for the incident,

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:31.000
...stating that, acting in accord with the laws of the universe, he will "cleanse" the human race.

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:33.180
This can't be...

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:38.060
We know that Enkidu carried off ten Gilgamesh experimental subjects.

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:42.190
You ought to know better than anyone what fearsome things they are.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:44.950
I will ask once again:

00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:48.690
Did you have a relationship with Enkidu as his lover?

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:04.780
You finally decided to come out?

00:20:06.520 --> 00:20:08.310
Because I could hear the piano.

00:20:09.590 --> 00:20:11.450
How unfortunate that it was only me.

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:18.900
Alcohol is convenient, isn't it?

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:20.630
Because it lets us pretend things never happened.

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:23.530
You mean memories of the distant past?

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:24.560
Yes...

00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:33.340
And things like this too...

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:56.100
You look prettiest when you smile.

00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:16.320
My lady, what might be the matter?

00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:19.920
Didn't Tatsuya come past you just now?

00:21:20.690 --> 00:21:24.630
No, my lady. Master Tatsuya remains in the infirmary.

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:25.760
What?

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:28.930
Staying close by Miss Kiyoko's side.

00:21:30.900 --> 00:21:32.100
My lady...

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:36.000
It couldn't be...

00:23:24.820 --> 00:23:26.080
Come on, this way.

00:23:26.820 --> 00:23:30.990
In this salon, there are lots of hard-to-get, valuable books.

00:23:30.990 --> 00:23:33.290
I'll read to you as much as you want.

00:23:33.290 --> 00:23:35.420
If you have a request, whatever it is, tell me.

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:37.090
What's wrong?

00:23:37.660 --> 00:23:38.860
Wait!

00:23:39.630 --> 00:23:40.890
This place is kind of...

00:23:42.200 --> 00:23:43.390
Sorry...

00:23:49.740 --> 00:23:51.010
Yes, Ma'am!

00:23:51.010 --> 00:23:53.600
Sorry! It's me. It's Toru, Ma'am!
